# What a project keeps out of its history: everything the editor makes again by
# itself, and everything that is true of this machine rather than of the game.
# Copied into a new project when it is created - see ProjectCreation.CopyGitIgnore.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The editor's own
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Thumbnails, mesh previews, undo journals, the layout of your docks, cloud.db.
# Rebuilt on open, and no two people want each other's.
.rinten/

# Compiled resources: everything beside its definition with _c on the end, and
# the sidecars beside those - picture.png.tex_c, picture.png.tex_c.bc,
# thing.mdl_c, thing.mdl_c.baked, scenes/main.scene_c. The editor compiles
# whatever it finds uncompiled when it scans, so a fresh clone builds its own.
#
# One exception, and it matters: a model with no art file behind it - one built
# in the model editor, or ported - has nothing to be rebuilt from, so its _c is
# the only copy there is. Keep those: git add -f the/model.mdl_c
#
# By these three shapes rather than *_c.* - a picture of yours called
# shield_c.png is not a compiled anything.
*_c
*_c.bc
*_c.baked

# On purpose NOT ignored: *.scene_d, the scene's binary half. It is written by
# the scene itself when you save, not compiled from anything, and a scene
# without it opens empty.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written for this machine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The solution, the C# projects and their launch settings are generated every
# time the project opens, and they carry absolute paths to the engine on this
# computer - committing them means a diff on every open and a broken path on
# everybody else's. Yours to keep anyway? git add -f the/file
*.slnx
*.csproj
**/Properties/launchSettings.json

# Written by the editor: file associations and the shader include paths, which
# are again this machine's.
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Exported games - every platform, every build.
Builds/

# Libraries the project fetches for itself, named in the .rinproj.
Libraries/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
TestResults/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Odds and ends
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
